We need to identify audit consistency bug: audit records success even when write fails. In ProfileService.changeStatus, they have try { ... } finally { auditRepository.recordSuccess(...); }. The finally runs regardless of exception. If profileRepository.require or save throws exception, the audit still records success, causing inconsistency. Should record success only if operation succeeded. So need to move audit call to after successful save, perhaps in try block after save, and ensure finally does not record success. Could use try { ...; audit... } catch { ... } or separate finally for cleanup not audit. The fix: move audit call into try block after save, and add catch to possibly record failure. Or use try { ...; audit... } finally { if (success) audit... }. Simplest: move audit call out of finally, put inside try after save, and add catch to handle errors. Also maybe record failure in catch.

Thus patch: modify ProfileService.changeStatus to:

public void changeStatus(long profileId, String newStatus) {
    try {
        Profile profile = profileRepository.require(profileId);
        profile.setStatus(newStatus);
        profileRepository.save(profile);
        auditRepository.recordSuccess("PROFILE_STATUS_CHANGED", profileId);
    } catch (Exception e) {
        // optionally log or record failure
        auditRepository.recordFailure("PROFILE_STATUS_CHANGED", profileId, e);
        throw e;
    }
}

But we only have AuditRepository with recordSuccess; maybe we add recordFailure later but not needed for bug fix. At minimum, ensure success only recorded on success.

